{"orgCode":"4250","name":"California Children and Families Commission","agencyCode":"4000","agencyName":"Health and Human Services","description":"The California Children and Families Commission, commonly known as First 5 California, was established by the California Children and Families Act of 1998 (Proposition 10) with a mission to:\n\nConvene, partner in, support, and help lead the movement to create and implement a comprehensive, integrated, and coordinated system for California's children prenatal through age five and their families. Promote, support, and optimize early childhood development.","totals":{"amounts":{"py":277873,"cy":264403,"by":264403},"positions":{"py":0,"cy":0,"by":0}},"programs":{"id":"exp/4000/4250","kind":"department","name":"California Children and Families Commission","code":"4250","amounts":{"py":277873,"cy":264403,"by":264403},"positions":{"py":0,"cy":0,"by":0},"byFundType":{"special":{"py":277873,"cy":264403,"by":264403}},"children":[{"id":"exp/4000/4250/3950","kind":"program","name":"California Children and Families Commission","code":"3950","amounts":{"py":277873,"cy":264403,"by":264403},"byFundType":{"special":{"py":277873,"cy":264403,"by":264403}},"positions":{"py":0,"cy":0,"by":0},"description":"3950 - CALIFORNIA CHILDREN AND FAMILIES COMMISSION\n\nThe Commission allocates funding for initiatives and projects consistent with the California Children and Families Act of 1998. The Commission is responsible for the implementation of comprehensive and integrated services, systems and solutions designed to provide information and services promoting, supporting, and improving the early childhood development of children through the age of five years. These initiatives and projects address recognized needs related to children's school readiness, including community awareness, education, nurturing, child care, social services, health care and research.","extra":{"byAppropriationType":{"State Operations":{"py":1507,"cy":1747,"by":1747},"Loca